Two dippers $D_{1}$ and $D_{2}$ are used to produce identical waves on the surface of water, as illustrated in Fig. 6.3.
{{figure:figure_6_3.png}}
Point P is 7.2 cm from $D_{1}$ and 11.2 cm from $D_{2}$. The wavelength of the waves is 1.6 cm. The phase difference between the waves produced at $D_{1}$ and $D_{2}$ is zero.
